      "content": "The pitch increase can be attributed to the specific design of the turbocharger's compressor wheel. As the compressor wheel accelerates, the impeller blades encounter a stronger-than-usual dynamic pressure, causing the sound to rise in pitch. This phenomenon is typically more pronounced when boost pressure transfers rapidly through the system, often at the point where the turbocharger is directly connected to its fuel and engine fuel system. Additionally, the sharp change in air density, typically near or just above the turbine bypass point, can also introduce sharp discontinuities in airflow, which contribute to the whistling sound.",
